 systemd-sysv | systemd,
Description: cron management for Proxmox VE, as a proxmod extension
 Adds cron management to the Proxmox VE web interface: a Cron tab in the
 datacenter view for cluster-wide entries, a Cron tab in the node view for
 host entries, a read-only inventory of every other cron entry on the host,
 and per-run history with captured output.
 .
 Job definitions are rendered into real files under /etc/cron.d and executed by
 the system's own cron. There is no new daemon and no scheduler of its own:
 what an administrator sees with cat is what runs. Cluster definitions live in
 /etc/pve/proxmod/cron.cfg and are replicated by pmxcfs, so a job created on one
 node appears on the others within a minute.
 .
 Run tracking and captured output are written to the systemd journal as
 structured entries, which means retention, rotation and access are the host's
 existing settings rather than a log store this package invents. Nothing about
 a job running depends on that history existing.
 .
 Other extensions can register job types, manage jobs through a Perl client, and
 contribute editor forms through a documented JavaScript namespace. A job created
 that way can be enabled and disabled by an administrator but not edited or
 removed behind the owning extension's back.
 .
 This package is not standalone: it is a proxmod extension and does nothing
 without proxmod installed.
